.TH TMELD 1 "July 2026" "tmeld 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmeld \- Meld, in your terminal: TUI diff and merge tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmeld
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIPATH\fR [\fIPATH\fR [\fIPATH\fR]]
[\fB\-\-diff\fR \fIPATH\fR...]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmeld
is a faithful terminal port of the GNOME Meld visual diff and merge
tool, using Meld's own diff engine. It supports two- and three-way
file comparison and merging, folder comparison, and a version-control
working-copy view \(em over plain SSH.
.PP
The comparison type is chosen from the arguments, as in Meld: two or
three files open a file comparison (three-way argument order is
\fILOCAL MERGED REMOTE\fR, the git mergetool convention \(em the middle
pane is the merged file); two or three directories open a folder
comparison; a single path opens the version-control view of the
enclosing working copy (git, mercurial, bzr, svn, darcs, cvs).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Write middle-pane saves to \fIFILE\fR instead of the middle path
(three-way file comparison only, like \fBmeld \-o\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-diff " " \fIPATH\fR...
Open an extra comparison tab for 1-3 paths. May be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fIname\fR
Color scheme: \fBmeld-base\fR (default) or \fBmeld-dark\fR, both using
Meld's exact palette.
.TP
.BR \-\-graphics " " \fImode\fR
Pixel linkmap protocol: \fBauto\fR (default; probes the terminal at
startup), \fBnone\fR, \fBsixel\fR or \fBkitty\fR. On capable terminals
the gutter between panes shows Meld's anti-aliased connector curves
and the overview map gains pixel resolution.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
Keybindings follow Meld: Alt+Down/Alt+Up (or Ctrl+D/Ctrl+E) navigate
changes, Alt+Left/Alt+Right push chunks, Alt+Shift+arrows pull,
Alt+Delete deletes a chunk, Ctrl+K/Ctrl+J navigate conflicts, Alt+M
merges all non-conflicting chunks, Ctrl+S saves, Ctrl+W closes a tab,
Ctrl+R or F5 refreshes, Ctrl+Q quits. In the version-control view,
\fBc\fR commits and \fBr\fR reverts. See the README for the full
table. On macOS terminals, configure Option to send Esc+.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For three-way comparisons the exit status is 0 only if the merged
(middle) file was saved, satisfying the git mergetool contract; other
comparisons exit 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Compare two files:
.B tmeld a.py b.py
.TP
Resolve a merge as git mergetool (with trustExitCode):
.B tmeld $LOCAL $MERGED $REMOTE
.TP
Compare folders:
.B tmeld dirA/ dirB/
.TP
Working-copy status view:
.B tmeld .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR meld (1),
.BR git-mergetool (1)
.PP
Full documentation: https://github.com/mitnits/tmeld
